// EXPECT-FAIL: typecheck
// `const` is the enforced-immutable half of the two-keyword model (`let` = mutable variable,
// `const` = constant; `var` is removed). Reassigning a `const` binding is a hard sema error
// (infer.zig records it, shadow.zig rejects with a located diagnostic). `let` stays reassignable,
// and mutating THROUGH a const reference (`const xs = List(); xs.push(1)`) is allowed — only a bare
// rebinding of the const itself is rejected.
@test
fn t(): void {
    const x = 5;
    x = 6;
}
